se is seen.","Days-overdue buckets: the assumptions disagree (ASM-5: 7–30/31–60/61–90/90+; ASM-14: 7–14/15–30/30+). This spec uses ASM-5 with the upper bucket starting at 91 so buckets don't overlap. The client needs to confirm.","Email provider: ASM-6 (transactional provider with bounce webhooks) is used over ASM-12 (existing SMTP relay), because Q-8 needs later bounces reported back, and a plain SMTP relay can't give that reliably.","Email wording: ASM-8 and ASM-15 agree that the template is fixed and stored in config. We draft it, the client approves it, and the client supplies the from address.","Overdue threshold (default 7) and business timezone are app settings (ASM-3, ASM-10, ASM-9, ASM-11).","Days overdue counts whole calendar days from the due date to today in the business timezone (ASM-4), so an invoice first appears on the list with days overdue = 7.","A send blocked because the customer has no email address is rejected before any provider call and is not recorded in reminder history. Q-3's 'every attempt' is read as every attempt that reaches the provider.","The double-submit window is 60 s per invoice (ASM-13). It counts from the previous request that reached the provider, whatever its outcome.","Reminders can be sent from both the overdue list and the invoice detail screen (ASM-16).","Provider error HTTP code 502 and missing-email code 422 are proposed status codes. If the client's API has its own error conventions, those win."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"p95 response time ≤ 1000 ms with 5,000 open invoices and 500 customers","text":"The overdue list endpoint responds quickly for the expected data size, with or without filters."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"Provider call timeout of 10 s; endpoint returns within 12 s in 100% of requests","text":"The send reminder endpoint does not hang on a slow email provider."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"0 occurrences of customer email addresses in log output during the full acceptance test run","text":"Customer email 