"then":"the invoice is not in the response","when":"an authenticated staff user calls GET the overdue list endpoint"},{"given":"an invoice row in Postgres, recorded before the request","id":"AC-1.5","level":"api","then":"the invoice row in the database is byte-for-byte unchanged (no status or updated-at column written)","when":"the overdue list endpoint is called and returns that invoice"},{"given":"business timezone UTC+10, an open invoice with due date 2026-10-01, and the server clock at 2026-10-07T15:00Z (2026-10-08 01:00 local)","id":"AC-1.6","level":"api","then":"the invoice is in the response","when":"an authenticated staff user calls GET the overdue list endpoint"}],"ears":"The Invoice Reminders API shall treat an invoice as overdue only when its status is not paid or closed and the current date in the configured business timezone is on or after its due date plus the configured overdue threshold (default 7 days), working this out at query time without writing any status to the invoice record.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-2","Q-4","Q-6","ASM-1","ASM-2","ASM-3","ASM-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"today is 2026-10-20 in the business timezone and an open invoice INV-100 for customer 'Crumb & Co', amount 250.00, due 2026-10-01","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"the entry for INV-100 has invoice number INV-100, customer 'Crumb & Co', amount 250.00, due date 2026-10-01 and days overdue 19","when":"an authenticated staff user calls GET the overdue list endpoint"},{"given":"3 overdue invoices and 2 invoices that are not overdue","id":"AC-2.2","level":"api","then":"the response contains exactly the 3 overdue invoices","when":"an authenticated staff user calls GET the overdue list endpoint"}],"ears":"When an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list, the Invoice Reminders API shall return every overdue invoice with its invoice number, customer name, amount, due date and days overdue, where days overdue is the number of whole days between the due date and today in the business timezone.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-6","ASM-4","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"no authentication token","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"the response is HTTP 401 and contains no invoice data","when":"GET the overdue list endpoint is called"},{"given":"an expired or invalid token and an overdue invoice","id":"AC-3.2","level":"api","then":"the response is HTTP 401, the email provider receives no call, and no reminder history row is created","when":"POST the send reminder endpoint is called for that invoice"},{"given":"no authentication token","id":"AC-3.3","level":"api","then":"the response is HTTP 401","when":"GET the invoice detail endpoint is called"}],"ears":"If a request to the overdue list, invoice detail or send reminder endpoint has no valid staff authentication from the existing API's authentication, then the Invoice Reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 401 and send no email.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"overdue invoices for customer A (2) and customer B (3)","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"the response contains exactly customer A's 2 overdue invoices","when":"an authenticated staff user calls GET the overdue list endpoint filtered by customer A"},{"given":"customer C has no overdue invoices","id":"AC-4.2","level":"api","then":"the response is HTTP 200 with an empty list","when":"the overdue list is requested filtered by customer C"}],"ears":"When the overdue list is requested with a customer filter, the Invoice Reminders API shall return only overdue invoices belonging to that customer.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"overdue invoices that are 7, 30, 31, 60, 61, 90 and 91 days overdue","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"only the 7 and 30 day invoices are returned","when":"the overdue list is requested with bucket 7–30"},{"given":"the same invoices","id":"AC-5.2","level":"api","then":"only the 91 day invoice is returned","when":"the overdue list is requested with bucket 91+"},{"given":"overdue invoices for customers A and B, with A having one 40-day and one 10-day invoice","id":"AC-5.3","level":"api","then":"only A's 40-day invoice is returned","when":"the overdue list is requested with customer A and bucket 31–60"},{"given":"any data","id":"AC-5.4","level":"api","then":"the response is HTTP 400","when":"the overdue list is requested with a bucket value that is not one of the four buckets"}],"ears":"When the overdue list is requested with a days-overdue filter, the Invoice Reminders API shall return only overdue invoices whose days overdue fall in the chosen bucket, the buckets being 7–30, 31–60, 61–90 and 91 or more days.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","ASM-5","ASM-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"overdue invoice INV-100, amount 250.00, due 2026-10-01, whose customer email is accounts@crumb.example, and a stubbed email provider","id":"AC-6.1","level":"api","then":"the provider stub receives exactly one send request addressed to accounts@crumb.example whose body contains 'INV-100', '250.00' and '2026-10-01', and the response is a success status","when":"an authenticated staff user calls POST the send reminder endpoint for INV-100"},{"given":"the template in configuration is changed to a different subject line","id":"AC-6.2","level":"api","then":"the provider stub receives the new subject line","when":"a reminder is sent"}],"ears":"When an authenticated staff user sends a reminder for an overdue invoice, the Invoice Reminders API shall send one email through the configured transactional email provider to the single email address on the invoice's customer record, using the configured template and containing the invoice number, amount and due date.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","Q-7","ASM-6","ASM-7","ASM-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"an overdue invoice whose customer record email field is empty","id":"AC-7.1","level":"api","then":"the response is HTTP 422 with an error stating the customer has no email address, the provider stub receives no call, and no reminder history row is created","when":"an authenticated staff user calls POST the send reminder endpoint for it"}],"ears":"If the customer record of the invoice has no email address, then the Invoice Reminders API shall reject the send reminder request with HTTP 422 and an error message saying the customer has no email address, without calling the email provider.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-7","ASM-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"staff user 'jo@bakery.example' and a provider stub that accepts the send","id":"AC-8.1","level":"api","then":"a reminder history row exists for INV-100 with sender jo@bakery.example, timestamp 2026-10-08T09:00:00Z (±5 s), status 'sent' and empty failure reason","when":"jo sends a reminder for INV-100 at 2026-10-08T09:00:00Z"},{"given":"two reminders already sent for INV-100 more than 60 seconds apart","id":"AC-8.2","level":"api","then":"two separate rows exist, one for each attempt","when":"the reminder history for INV-100 is read"}],"ears":"When a reminder send attempt is made to the email provider, the Invoice Reminders API shall store a reminder history record holding the invoice, the sending staff user, the UTC timestamp of the attempt and a delivery status of sent or failed with a failure reason.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"an overdue invoice INV-100 and a provider stub that rejects the send with reason 'invalid recipient'","id":"AC-9.1","level":"api","then":"the response is an HTTP 502 error with reason 'invalid recipient', and a reminder history row for INV-100 has status 'failed' and reason 'invalid recipient'","when":"an authenticated staff user calls POST the send reminder endpoint for INV-100"},{"given":"the failed attempt from AC-9.1","id":"AC-9.2","level":"api","then":"INV-100 is still in the response","when":"the overdue list is requested"},{"given":"a provider stub that does not respond within the provider timeout","id":"AC-9.3","level":"api","then":"the attempt is recorded as 'failed' with a timeout reason and an error response is returned","when":"a reminder is sent"}],"ears":"If the email provider returns an error when a reminder is sent, then the Invoice Reminders API shall record the attempt as failed with the provider's error reason, return an error response containing that reason, and leave the invoice on the overdue list.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","Q-3","Q-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"a reminder for INV-100 recorded as 'sent' with provider message id 'm-1'","id":"AC-10.1","level":"api","then":"the webhook returns HTTP 200 and the reminder history row now has status 'failed' and reason 'mailbox does not exist', and INV-100 is still on the overdue list","when":"the provider bounce webhook endpoint receives a correctly signed bounce event for 'm-1' with reason 'mailbox does not exist'"},{"given":"no reminder exists with provider message id 'm-unknown'","id":"AC-10.2","level":"api","then":"the webhook returns HTTP 200 and no reminder history row changes","when":"a correctly signed bounce event for 'm-unknown' is received"}],"ears":"When the email provider reports a bounce for a reminder previously recorded as sent, the Invoice Reminders API shall change that reminder history record's status to failed with the bounce reason given by the provider.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","Q-8","ASM-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"a reminder recorded as 'sent' with provider message id 'm-1'","id":"AC-11.1","level":"api","then":"the response is HTTP 401 and the reminder history row still has status 'sent'","when":"the bounce webhook endpoint receives a bounce event for 'm-1' with a missing or wrong signature"}],"ears":"If a bounce webhook request fails the email provider's signature verification, then the Invoice Reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 401 and change no reminder history record.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","ASM-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"a reminder for INV-100 sent at 09:00:00","id":"AC-12.1","level":"api","then":"the response is HTTP 409, the provider stub has received exactly one send in total, and one reminder history row exists","when":"a second send reminder request for INV-100 arrives at 09:00:30"},{"given":"a reminder for INV-100 sent at 09:00:00","id":"AC-12.2","level":"api","then":"the request succeeds, the provider stub has received two sends, and two history rows exist","when":"another send reminder request for INV-100 arrives at 09:01:01"},{"given":"a reminder for INV-100 sent at 09:00:00","id":"AC-12.3","level":"api","then":"the INV-200 request succeeds","when":"a send reminder request for a different invoice INV-200 arrives at 09:00:10"},{"given":"two send reminder requests for INV-100 sent at the same moment","id":"AC-12.4","level":"api","then":"exactly one reaches the provider and the other returns HTTP 409","when":"both are processed"}],"ears":"If a send reminder request arrives for an invoice within 60 seconds of a previous send reminder request for the same invoice that reached the email provider, then the Invoice Reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 409 without calling the email provider or recording a reminder history record.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-5","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"INV-100 with amount 250.00, due 2026-10-01, one 'sent' attempt by jo at 2026-10-08T09:00Z and one 'failed' attempt by sam at 2026-10-09T10:00Z with reason 'invalid recipient'","id":"AC-13.1","level":"api","then":"the response has amount 250.00, due date 2026-10-01 and history [sam 2026-10-09T10:00Z failed 'invalid recipient', jo 2026-10-08T09:00Z sent] in that order","when":"an authenticated staff user calls GET the invoice detail endpoint for INV-100"},{"given":"an invoice with no reminders","id":"AC-13.2","level":"api","then":"the response has an empty reminder history","when":"its detail is requested"}],"ears":"When an authenticated staff user requests an invoice's detail, the Invoice Reminders API shall return the invoice's amount and due date and its full reminder history, newest first, with each attempt's sender, timestamp, delivery status and failure reason.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-4","I-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"a signed-in staff user and 3 overdue invoices","id":"AC-14.1","level":"manual","then":"a table shows 3 rows with invoice number, customer, amount, due date and days overdue, plus customer and days-overdue filter controls","when":"the user opens the overdue list screen"},{"given":"the overdue list screen with a slow provider stub","id":"AC-14.2","level":"manual","then":"the button is disabled after the first click until the request completes, and only one email is sent","when":"the user clicks Send reminder on a row and clicks it again straight away"},{"given":"a provider stub that rejects sends with 'invalid recipient'","id":"AC-14.3","level":"manual","then":"the screen shows the failure with reason 'invalid recipient' and the row stays in the table","when":"the user clicks Send reminder on a row"}],"ears":"The overdue list screen shall show the overdue invoices in a table with invoice number, customer, amount, due date and days overdue, a customer filter, a days-overdue bucket filter, and a Send reminder button on each row that is disabled while its request is in progress and shows the success or failure reason when it completes.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-5","I-4","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"INV-100 with one sent and one failed reminder","id":"AC-15.1","level":"manual","then":"the screen shows amount, due date and both history entries, with the failed one showing its failure reason","when":"a signed-in staff user opens the invoice detail screen for INV-100"},{"given":"the invoice detail screen for an overdue invoice","id":"AC-15.2","level":"manual","then":"a new history entry appears on the screen with the user's name, the current time and its delivery status","when":"the user clicks Send reminder"}],"ears":"The invoice detail screen shall show the invoice's amount, due date and reminder history including each attempt's sender, time, delivery status and failure reason, and a Send reminder button.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","I-3","I-4","ASM-16"]}],"suggestions":["Reject send reminder requests on the server for invoices that are not overdue (for example, already paid), since the detail screen may show the button for any invoice.","Show the latest reminder date and delivery status as a column on the overdue list so staff can see failures without opening each invoice.","Restrict reminder sending to a staff role if the client's auth has roles, given the payments/PII risk tags.","Add a per-user rate limit on the send reminder endpoint (for example, 100 per hour) to limit mass emailing from a compromised account.","Also handle provider 'spam complaint' and 'blocked' events as delivery failures if the chosen provider reports them.","Add audit logging of who viewed invoice detail, if the client needs PII access tracking."]},{"assumptions":["No repository was available (current-behaviour has no claims), so every requirement is ADDED. Invoices and customers are read from the client's existing .NET 8 API and Postgres database (ASM-1).","Endpoint names are proposals for test authors: GET /api/invoices/overdue?customerId=&daysOverdue=7-30|31-60|61-90|90plus, GET /api/invoices/{id}, POST /api/invoices/{id}/reminders, POST /api/email-provider/events (webhook).","The days-overdue ranges follow ASM-5 (7–30, 31–60, 61–90, 90+). ASM-14 (7–14, 15–30, 30+) conflicts with it and overlaps at day 30, so it was not used.","The email channel follows ASM-6 (a transactional provider with a bounce webhook), because Q-8 requires bounces reported back by the provider. ASM-12 (an SMTP relay) conflicts with it and would not report bounces.","The overdue threshold is an app setting with default 7 (ASM-3 and ASM-10 agree). 'Today' uses the configured business timezone (ASM-9 and ASM-11 agree).","The reminder wording and from address come from a configured template approved by the client (ASM-8 and ASM-15 are combined).","A request blocked because the email address is missing (REQ-6) is not a delivery attempt, so it creates no reminder history entry.","A request rejected as a duplicate (REQ-10) creates no history entry. The 60-second window counts from the previous accepted request for the same invoice.","The webhook is authenticated by checking the provider's signature against a configured secret. It does not use staff authentication.","The sender recorded in history is the identity of the authenticated user from the existing API authentication."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"p95 ≤ 1000 ms with 5,000 open invoices and 500 customers","text":"Overdue list endpoint response time with filters applied"},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"p95 ≤ 5 s; provider call timeout 10 s, after which the attempt is recorded as failed","text":"Send-reminder endpoint response time including the provider call"},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"≥ 99% of valid bounce events applied within 60 s of receipt","text":"Bounce webhook events are reflected in reminder history"},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"0 occurrences of customer email addresses in application logs during the test run","text":"Customer email addresses (PII) are not written to application logs"},{"id":"NFR-5","metric":"0 duplicate provider send calls when 10 concurrent requests for the same invoice arrive within 1 s","text":"No duplicate emails come from double submits"}],"outOfScope":["Payments and marking invoices paid (the paid/closed status is only read from existing invoice data)","Customer logins or customer-facing screens","SMS reminders","Automatic or scheduled reminders (all reminders are sent by staff)","Role-based permissions beyond 'any authenticated staff user'","Writing an overdue status onto invoice records","Editing customer email addresses","Multiple email addresses per customer"],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"threshold 7, business timezone set, today is 2026-10-15 in that timezone, open invoice A due 2026-10-08 and open invoice B due 2026-10-09","id":"AC-1.1","level":"api","then":"invoice A is in the response and invoice B is not","when":"an authenticated staff user calls GET the overdue list endpoint"},{"given":"invoice C due 2026-09-01 with status paid and invoice D due 2026-09-01 with status closed, today 2026-10-15","id":"AC-1.2","level":"api","then":"neither C nor D is in the response","when":"the overdue list is requested"},{"given":"open invoice A due 2026-10-08 is on the overdue list and its status is then changed to paid in the invoice data","id":"AC-1.3","level":"api","then":"invoice A is no longer in the response, with no other action needed","when":"the overdue list is requested again"},{"given":"the overdue threshold setting is changed to 10 and today is 2026-10-15","id":"AC-1.4","level":"api","then":"an open invoice due 2026-10-05 is included and an open invoice due 2026-10-06 is not","when":"the overdue list is requested"},{"given":"business timezone is UTC+10 and the server clock is 2026-10-14T15:00Z (2026-10-15 01:00 local)","id":"AC-1.5","level":"api","then":"an open invoice due 2026-10-08 is included","when":"the overdue list is requested"},{"given":"an invoice row in Postgres before the overdue list is requested","id":"AC-1.6","level":"api","then":"the invoice row is byte-for-byte unchanged (no status or other column written)","when":"the overdue list is requested"}],"ears":"When the overdue list is requested, the invoice reminders API shall include every invoice that is not paid or closed and for which today's date in the configured business timezone is on or after its due date plus the configured overdue threshold (default 7 days).","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-2","Q-4","Q-6","ASM-1","ASM-2","ASM-3","ASM-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"today 2026-10-15 and open invoice INV-100 for customer 'Crumb & Co', amount 250.00, due 2026-10-01","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"the INV-100 item has invoiceNumber INV-100, customer 'Crumb & Co', amount 250.00, dueDate 2026-10-01 and daysOverdue 14","when":"the overdue list is requested"}],"ears":"When the overdue list is requested, the invoice reminders API shall return for each overdue invoice its invoice number, customer name, amount, due date and days overdue counted as whole days since the due date.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-6","ASM-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"overdue invoices for customer X (2 invoices) and customer Y (1 invoice)","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"exactly the 2 invoices of customer X are returned","when":"the overdue list is requested filtered by customer X"}],"ears":"When the overdue list is requested with a customer filter, the invoice reminders API shall return only overdue invoices belonging to that customer.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"overdue invoices with daysOverdue 7, 30, 31, 60, 61, 90 and 91","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"7–30 returns 7 and 30; 31–60 returns 31 and 60; 61–90 returns 61 and 90; 90+ returns 91","when":"the overdue list is requested with each range in turn"},{"given":"overdue invoices for customers X and Y with daysOverdue 10 and 40 each","id":"AC-4.2","level":"api","then":"only customer X's 40-day invoice is returned","when":"the overdue list is requested with customer X and range 31–60"}],"ears":"When the overdue list is requested with a days-overdue filter, the invoice reminders API shall return only overdue invoices whose days overdue fall in the chosen range of 7–30, 31–60, 61–90 or more than 90 days.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","ASM-4","ASM-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"overdue invoice INV-100 (amount 250.00, due 2026-10-01) whose customer email is accounts@crumb.example, and a stub email provider","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"the stub provider receives exactly one send request addressed to accounts@crumb.example whose body contains 'INV-100', '250.00' and '2026-10-01', and the API returns a success status","when":"staff user 'sam' calls POST the send-reminder endpoint for INV-100"},{"given":"a reminder for INV-100 was sent more than 60 seconds ago","id":"AC-5.2","level":"api","then":"a second email is sent to the provider and the request succeeds","when":"staff call the send-reminder endpoint for INV-100 again"}],"ears":"When an authenticated staff user requests a reminder for an overdue invoice whose customer has an email address, the invoice reminders API shall send one email through the email provider to the customer's email address containing the invoice number, amount and due date.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","Q-1","Q-7","ASM-6","ASM-7","ASM-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"overdue invoice INV-200 whose customer record has an empty email field, and a stub email provider","id":"AC-6.1","level":"api","then":"the API returns a 4xx error whose message says the customer email address is missing and the stub provider receives no request","when":"staff call the send-reminder endpoint for INV-200"}],"ears":"If the customer of the invoice has no email address, then the invoice reminders API shall reject the reminder request with an error stating the email address is missing and send no email.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","Q-7","ASM-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"the stub provider accepts the email","id":"AC-7.1","level":"api","then":"a reminder history row exists for INV-100 with sender 'sam', timestamp 2026-10-15T09:30:00Z (±5s) and status 'sent'","when":"staff user 'sam' sends a reminder for INV-100 at 2026-10-15T09:30:00Z"},{"given":"INV-100 has had 3 reminder attempts","id":"AC-7.2","level":"api","then":"the response lists all 3 history entries, newest first, each with sender, timestamp and status","when":"the invoice detail endpoint is called for INV-100"}],"ears":"When a reminder send is attempted, the invoice reminders API shall store a reminder history entry holding the invoice, the authenticated staff user who sent it, the UTC timestamp, and a delivery status of sent or failed with a failure reason.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"the stub provider returns an error 'mailbox rejected' for the send","id":"AC-8.1","level":"api","then":"the API returns an error, a history row exists for INV-100 with status 'failed' and reason containing 'mailbox rejected', and INV-100 is still returned by the overdue list","when":"staff send a reminder for overdue invoice INV-100"}],"ears":"If the email provider returns an error when a reminder is sent, then the invoice reminders API shall record the attempt as failed with the provider's error reason, return an error to the caller, and leave the invoice on the overdue list.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","Q-3","Q-8","ASM-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"a history entry for INV-100 with status 'sent' and provider message id 'msg-1'","id":"AC-9.1","level":"api","then":"the history entry for 'msg-1' has status 'failed' and reason 'mailbox does not exist', and INV-100 remains on the overdue list","when":"a validly signed bounce event for 'msg-1' with reason 'mailbox does not exist' is posted to the provider webhook endpoint"},{"given":"a bounce event whose signature does not verify against the configured provider secret","id":"AC-9.2","level":"api","then":"the endpoint returns 401 and no history entry changes","when":"it is posted to the provider webhook endpoint"}],"ears":"When the email provider reports a bounce for a previously sent reminder, the invoice reminders API shall change that reminder's history entry to failed with the bounce reason.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","Q-8","ASM-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"a stub email provider and overdue invoice INV-100","id":"AC-10.1","level":"api","then":"the first succeeds, the second returns 409 Conflict, the provider receives exactly one send request and only one history entry is stored","when":"two send-reminder requests for INV-100 are made 2 seconds apart"},{"given":"a reminder request for INV-100 was made 10 seconds ago","id":"AC-10.2","level":"api","then":"the INV-101 request succeeds","when":"a reminder request for a different invoice INV-101 is made"}],"ears":"If a reminder request arrives for an invoice that already had a reminder request within the previous 60 seconds, then the invoice reminders API shall reject it as a duplicate and send no email.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","Q-5","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"INV-100 with one 'sent' entry and one 'failed' entry with reason 'mailbox does not exist'","id":"AC-11.1","level":"api","then":"the response contains invoice number, customer, amount, due date and both entries, the failed one showing reason 'mailbox does not exist'","when":"the invoice detail endpoint is called for INV-100"}],"ears":"When the invoice detail is requested, the invoice reminders API shall return the invoice number, customer, amount, due date and the full reminder history including each delivery failure reason.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-4","I-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"no authentication token","id":"AC-12.1","level":"api","then":"each returns 401 with no invoice or customer data in the body, and the stub provider receives no request","when":"each of the overdue list, invoice detail and send-reminder endpoints is called"}],"ears":"If a request to the overdue list, invoice detail or send-reminder endpoint is not authenticated by the existing API authentication, then the invoice reminders API shall return 401 and return no invoice or customer data.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"a logged-in staff user and at least 3 overdue invoices","id":"AC-13.1","level":"manual","then":"a table shows invoice number, customer, amount, due date and days overdue per row, with a customer filter, a days-overdue range filter (7–30, 31–60, 61–90, 90+) and a 'Send reminder' button on each row","when":"the user opens the overdue list screen"},{"given":"the overdue list screen is open","id":"AC-13.2","level":"manual","then":"the button is disabled until the response arrives, then a success message or the error message (for example a missing email address) is shown for that row","when":"the user clicks 'Send reminder' on a row"}],"ears":"The overdue list screen shall show overdue invoices in a table with customer and days-overdue filters and a 'Send reminder' button on each row that is disabled while its request is in progress.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-5","Q-5","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"an invoice with one sent and one failed reminder","id":"AC-14.1","level":"manual","then":"amount, due date and both history entries (sender, time, status) are shown, the failed entry shows its reason, and a 'Send reminder' button is present","when":"a staff user opens its invoice detail screen"}],"ears":"The invoice detail screen shall show the invoice amount, due date, reminder history with sender, time and status, each delivery failure reason, and a 'Send reminder' button.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","I-3","I-4","ASM-16"]}],"suggestions":["Decide whether the send-reminder endpoint should reject invoices that are not currently overdue, for example when sent from the detail screen of a paid invoice. The request does not say.","Add a 'last reminded' date and a failed-delivery marker to overdue list rows so staff can see failures without opening the detail screen.","Make the days-overdue ranges configurable, or let them start at the configured threshold, so they stay consistent if the threshold changes from 7.","Add a retention or deletion policy for reminder history, since it holds customer email-related data (PII).","Record and show customer complaints and spam reports from the provider, as well as bounces."]}],"models":["claude-opus-5-5","claude-opus-5-5","claude-opus-5-5"],"notes":["No OpenAI key: specify-other ran on claude-opus-5-5 (same family as the implementer)"]}